yesterday the Prime Minister failed to  put the matter to rest so today it fell  to the man himself his chief adviser  Dominic Cummins to explain why he left  London to stay in Durham at the peak of  the lockdown sorry I'm late  this the only apology as he sat out his  version of events in the gardens of  Downing Street I thought there was a  distinct probability that I had already  caught the disease I had a few  conflicting thoughts in my mind first I  was worried that if my wife and I were  both seriously ill possibly hospitalized  there was nobody in London that we could  reasonably ask to look after our child  and exposed themselves to kovat I  thought the best thing to do with all  the circumstances was to drive to an  isolated cottage on my father's farm I  thought that they could stay there for a  few weeks I could go back to work help  colleagues and everybody including the  general public would be safe I did not  ask the Prime Minister about this  decision he also confirmed that he did  take a trip to local beauty spot Barnard  Castle to check his eyesight was good  enough to drive rather than taking in  the sights we agreed that we should go  for a short drive to see if I could  drive safely we drove for roughly half  an hour and ended up on the outskirts of  Barney Castle town we walked about 10 to  15 metres from the car  to the river bank nearby we sat there  for about 15 minutes no offer of  resignation he doesn't think he's done  anything wrong I believe that all the  circumstances I behave reasonably and  legally I can understand that some  people will argue that I should have  stayed at my home in London throughout I  understand these views I know the  intense hardship and sacrifice that the  entire countries had to go through  however I respectfully disagree I  thought and I think today that the rules  including those regarding small children  and extreme circumstances allowed me to  exercise my judgement about the  situation I found myself in I accept of  course that there was room for  reasonable disagreement about this I  know that millions have endured awful  hardship including personal tragedies  over the past few months and people are  suffering every day and I know the  British people hate the idea of  unfairness a many angry and upset about  his conduct ordinary families have put  up with all kinds of risk  actions and hardships people not go into  funerals people not even going into  hospital when their kids have been  having cancer treatment why are you so  different I don't think I'm so different  and I don't think there's one rule for  me and one rule for other people I  looked at their and I knew what the  guidance was it talks about exceptional  circumstances with with small children  this isn't damage the Prime Minister it  has undermined your policy and it's  undermined public confidence in the  government how can you even countenance  at the moment staying on and not  resigning there is understandable anger  but a lot of that anger is based on  reports in the media that have not been  true and it's extremely regrettable but  you didn't think that you ought to check  with the Prime Minister knowing how that  might look how could you not even chat  with your boss that's a very reasonable  question and and I think a lot a lot of  people would say though that I ought to  have called the Prime Minister about it  we all had a million things on our  plates we were trying to do lots of  things I have to get on with things I  have to make make decisions and  sometimes I make do the right thing as  soon as I make mistakes in retrospect  you wish you chat with him fast I don't  know is there is there is it's the  honest truth about that particular thing  maybe I should have done and I made that  judgment in a very short period of time  in very extreme circumstances and as I  said I'd be I thought at the time was  the right thing to do the Prime Minister  standing by his mom but acknowledging  not everyone feels the way he does I do  regret the confusion and the anger and  the pain that people feel and that's why  I really did want people to understand  exactly what had happened  I tried yesterday to to explain my  version of what I heard from from  Dominic Cummings but you know obviously  I couldn't go into it in all the detail  and so that's why we had the the  statement and the the very extensive  questions that we did today your own  scientific advisers have  said by backing him you're undermining  your government's key public health  message at a time of crisis are you  compromising the government's response  to this pandemic because you can't cope  in number 10  without mr. Cummings the only reason  that were able to get this disease under  control  is because people have obeyed the  guidelines I do not believe that anybody  in number 10 has done anything to  undermine our our messaging often seen  but rarely heard but this long bank  holiday weekend people have talked about  little else  an anonymous aide has become a national  conversation mr. Cummings will hope he  did enough today to keep his job but  people are angry even if he does stay  the damage for Boris Johnson is already  done his People's Government has lost  many of its followers  Beth Rigby Sky News Westminster
 

